    // ---- Spirit Thief ----
    "project.spiritthief.back": "Back to portfolio",
    "project.spiritthief.title": "Spirit Thief",
    "project.spiritthief.tagline": "3D soulslike. Steal spirits, take on enemies, and escape the ruins of a fallen empire.",
    "project.spiritthief.link.itch": "Play on itch.io",
    "project.spiritthief.link.steam": "View on Steam",
    "project.spiritthief.link.github": "Code on GitHub",
    "project.spiritthief.about.heading": "About the project",
    "project.spiritthief.about.body": "Kassia Arnhild is the last survivor of her clan able to wield powers granted by nature spirits. Venture into the ruins of a fallen empire and reclaim the spirits that were stolen from your people long ago. Fight, jump, and overcome every challenge waiting for you on the floating islands of the fallen empire.\n\n3D soulslike with platforming elements. Built on a custom 3D engine written in C++ using OpenGL.\n\nThis is easily the biggest and most important project in my portfolio, with the largest team and the longest development cycle I've worked on.",
    "project.spiritthief.role.heading": "My role",
    "project.spiritthief.role.body": "On this project I worked across game engine development, gameplay, and the graphics engine.\n\nOn the game engine side, my contributions include: architecture, memory management, asset loading, profiling and optimization, level loading system, save system, Bullet Physics integration, ECS entity system, event system.\n\nOn the gameplay side: CCC (camera, character, controller), movement, an advanced combat system, enemy AI and navigation.\n\nFor the custom 3D engine built from scratch in C++ with OpenGL: static and skeletal mesh rendering, animation, cartoon lighting, shaders (water, trees, VFX), particle system, technical art, and visual identity.",
    "project.spiritthief.challenges.heading": "Technical challenges",
    "project.spiritthief.challenges.item1": "Building a complete game on a custom engine: defining the architecture, systems, tools, gameplay, components, and team organization.",
    "project.spiritthief.challenges.item2": "Building a custom 3D engine with rendering, skeletal animation, lighting, and shaders — all under a defined cartoon art direction and visual identity.",
    "project.spiritthief.challenges.item3": "Keeping performance under control through memory management, asset loading, profiling, and optimization on both the graphics and gameplay side, applying various industry-standard techniques.",
    "project.spiritthief.learned.heading": "What I learned",
    "project.spiritthief.learned.body": "This project taught me a huge amount across two very different areas: technical and organizational.\n\nOn the technical side, I learned to build a game engine from scratch, including rendering, animation, lighting, shaders, physics, AI, and gameplay systems. I learned to optimize and profile both a game engine and a full game to keep performance in check at every stage. These are key lessons in my growth as a programmer — thanks to all this, I now have a much deeper understanding of how every component of a modern game engine works, the kind of understanding you can only reach by building one yourself.\n\nOn the organizational side, I learned to work as part of a team through a long development cycle with a large team. I learned to organize tasks, set priorities, and coordinate with other team members to hit deadlines and goals.",
