    // ---- Mask Apito ----
    "project.maskapito.back": "Back to portfolio",
    "project.maskapito.title": "Mask Apito",
    "project.maskapito.award": "Global Game Jam Alicante 2026 Winner",
    "project.maskapito.tagline": "3D beat 'em all where you collect and combine masks with powers.",
    "project.maskapito.link.itch": "Play on itch.io",
    "project.maskapito.link.steam": "View on Steam",
    "project.maskapito.link.github": "Code on GitHub",
    "project.maskapito.about.heading": "About the project",
    "project.maskapito.about.body": "In Apito village, every child in the forest has a unique mask with its own power. Every child except one, who had a plain, boring mask with no power at all. He was bullied for it. The solution? Attack everyone in the village and rip their masks from their cold hands. Fight, collect masks, combine powers, and defeat them all.\n\n3D beat 'em all created during Global Game Jam Alicante 2026. The player collects and combines masks to stack powers, deckbuilder-style.",
    "project.maskapito.role.heading": "My role",
    "project.maskapito.role.body": "I was the lead gameplay developer, covering: combat mechanics; a mask system with different powers and modifiers that stack on top of each other; and a random, deckbuilder-style mask system.\n\nThis was the first combat system I designed using a Stick To Target (STT) approach, where the enemy to hit is picked automatically based on several criteria (nearest enemy, camera position, etc.). With this system combat feels much more automatic, letting you focus on fast attack combos rather than strategic positioning. I chose this approach because combat systems I'd designed before, like Spirit Thief, relied on less automatic mechanics that demanded a more precise, strategic playstyle. The idea here was to make something simpler and more frantic, where you basically mash buttons and chain combos. A complete departure from the more precise, Dark Souls-style mechanics I'd built up to that point.",
    "project.maskapito.challenges.heading": "Technical challenges",
    "project.maskapito.challenges.item1": "Designing a mask system that let powers stack and combine (attack speed, fire attacks, explosive hits, area attacks, etc.).",
    "project.maskapito.challenges.item2": "Building a simple, fun, and satisfying combat system using techniques I was less familiar with.",
    "project.maskapito.challenges.item3": "Integrating the core mechanics into a playable prototype within a tight time limit.",
    "project.maskapito.learned.heading": "What I learned",
    "project.maskapito.learned.body": "Even though it was just a game jam, this project felt like the culmination of a set of organizational skills I'd struggled with in the past. I learned to better manage scope given the time and team I had available. I learned to prioritize which elements to build first and which to leave for last, to guarantee a minimum viable product within a limited timeframe. Finally, I learned to judge how much time to invest in different elements, with a sharper sense of what's worth polishing and what's better left as is.",
    "project.maskapito.facts.heading": "Fact sheet",
    "project.maskapito.facts.engine.label": "Engine",
    "project.maskapito.facts.engine.value": "Unreal Engine 5 (Blueprints)",
